{
  "_": [
    "Lenses found in Paillard's own dated dealer price lists, hand-matched.",
    "",
    "Source: the Bolex dealer price lists scanned by Pacific Rim Camera.",
    "These are primary documents. Each gives a lens, Paillard's five-letter",
    "code and a price on a stated date, which is harder evidence than",
    "anything on the open web: a price in the May 1967 dealer list proves",
    "the lens was on sale in May 1967.",
    "",
    "Matched by hand, not by script. The scans are OCR'd and the columns",
    "interleave, so a code can end up printed next to the previous entry's",
    "description. Every row here was read back against the page. asPrinted",
    "is the document's own wording, kept so the match can be re-checked",
    "without opening the PDF.",
    "",
    "addCodes adds a code our extraction did not have, because Michael did",
    "not give one in the lens's name. Those are the valuable ones: a code is",
    "what is engraved on the barrel.",
    "",
    "",
    "A trap in the two 1970s lists, written down because it would publish a",
    "dealer's cost as a shop price. October 1976 prints its columns as",
    "Dealer Cost then Suggested Retail. January 1978 prints them the other",
    "way round, Suggested Retail then Dealer Net. Everything here is the",
    "retail figure, which is the second number in the 1976 list and the",
    "first in the 1978 one. Both headers were read off the rendered page.",
    "",
    "Re-run scripts/extract-lens-items.mjs after editing."
  ],
